The fix reinstates the original logic by ensuring that the call to `iommu_probe_device(dev)` only occurs if there are no existing errors (`!err`). This prevents the overwriting of the `-EPROBE_DEFER` error, allowing for proper error handling and maintaining the integrity of the device initialization process.

